	"A better name would've'd been HexIDE, it even rolls of the tongue. whatever man.",
	"'Rounded IDE cables provide no better performance.'",
	"Dilapidated",
	"Hex is so hot it would smoke cigarettes.",
	"On a Friday?",
	"Hex's per frame allocation budget maximum is 256b :-)",
	"A little bit choppy but overall not too bad!",
	"One line forward, two allocations backward.",
	"It's happy hour somewhere..",
	"Its like a Dell optiplex, but no not really (i forgot where i was going with that)",
	"Vibecoder? I hardly know her!",
	"Does anyone wanna implement Doom in HIDL?",
	"it's not the same w/out u.",
	"Yeah I ran out of ideas to put here...",
	"Optimising this made me implement tick skipping into Horizon...",
	"UI Compositing got my brain composting...",
	"the air in my room feels different without you",
	"Fuck it... UwU",
	"Fuck it... NuWu",
	"Oh the golorious burdern of genius...",
	"i hope you miss me..",
	"Guess who was single on Valentine's Day & Halloween :cry:",
	"idk man, that does NOT look like good code to me!",
	"Honestly, man, I wrote this because the VSCode extension exhausted me.",
	"Zopiclone doesn't work for my anymore, this sentence only took 2 minutes to type.",
	"Caching icons referenced in labels ended up saving over 1MB/frame in allocations...",
	"You should really take a break... I'm getting worried...",
	"It's always been a psyop",
	"This project started after a RAM consumption induced panic attack caused by VSCode.",
	"A muon hit my brain cell and then this code diarrhea happened...",
	"Nothing to be done.",
	"Damn, I should implement a generic Form contro- no.. w- winforms.. gdi... :skull:",
	"I blame Vyvanse for this.",
	"Here I am, stuck working with a bottom like you...",
	"asdf",
	"qwertyuiop",
	"F360>SW",
	"Did you know: my favourite ice cream flavour is vanilla?",
	"Did you know: the original Xbox had, at least, 3 internal cables?"
];

// A greeting that isn't the one up there already, there's no fun in being greeted the same way twice
let greeting = { shown: "" };
func greet(hex) {
	let next = math.pick(welcome_greetings);
	while (next == greeting.shown) {
		next = math.pick(welcome_greetings);
	}
	greeting.shown = next;
	hex.title_note(next);
}

// Hex calls this once it starts up, with what it lets an extension do. A greeting, another every minute, and a command
// in the palette for one straight away
func on_start(hex) {
	greet(hex);
	hex.every(60, greet);
	hex.command("Another greeting", greet);
}
